<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ivan Shishman</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1395">1395</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Ivan Šišman</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ivan Shishman was the last tsar of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/veliko-tarnovo">Tarnovo</a>, reigning from 1371 to 1395. A son of Ivan Alexander, he inherited a divided realm and became a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of the Ottoman sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murad-i">Murad I</a>. Tarnovo fell to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> in 1393, and he was captured and executed in 1395. Popular tradition made him a hero of resistance.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ivan-shishman.jpg" alt="Ivan Shishman" width="148" height="225" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:53_IoSisiman.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Basarab I's victory at the Battle of Posada in 1330 won independence from Charles I of Hungary; the first clash with the Ottomans came under Vladislav I, allied with <b>Ivan Shishman</b> of Bulgaria.</blockquote><a href="/empire/principality-of-wallachia">Principality of Wallachia · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Royal charters granting land and privileges to monasteries, among them <b>Ivan Shishman</b>'s charter to the Rila Monastery of 1378, survive as rare documents of Bulgarian administration.</blockquote><a href="/empire/second-bulgarian-empire">Second Bulgarian Empire · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>Tsar Ivan Alexander of the Second Bulgarian Empire made his younger son <b>Ivan Shishman</b> heir and gave his eldest, Ivan Sratsimir, the north-western region around Vidin.</blockquote><a href="/state/tsardom-of-vidin">Tsardom of Vidin</a></li></ul></section>
